# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

Sets the monthly spend limit of the organization with the Admin API key (`admin_api_key`), or removes it. The limit caps the API and Vibe consumption of the whole organization; a workspace spend limit, set in the Admin Panel, cannot exceed it. The Admin API needs an Enterprise plan and access granted by Mistral.

-> **Public preview at Mistral.** The Admin API is in public preview: Mistral can change its fields without a deprecation period, and following them may take a new release of the provider.

~> **Not verified against the live API.** This resource is tested against a fake of the Mistral API written from Mistral's documentation. No acceptance test has run against a Mistral organization yet: please report any difference with the live API in an issue.

~> **A limit below the usage stops the API.** When the organization reaches its monthly limit, Mistral can suspend its API access until the next month begins or an admin raises the limit.

## Amount

`amount` is a whole number in the billing currency of the organization, which `currency` gives: `500` means 500, not 500 cents. Set `no_monthly_limit = true`, without `amount`, to remove the limit. The API requires an amount even then: the provider sends the current limit with it.

The API reads the limit back as a number. A limit with a fractional part, which only a change outside Terraform could set, fails the refresh rather than being rounded.

## One per organization

An organization has one spend limit, which always exists: declare this resource once. Two of them, in one configuration or in two, would overwrite each other on every apply.

To avoid overwriting a limit set outside Terraform, the create fails when the organization already has a limit different from the configuration, and gives the `import` block that brings it under Terraform. A limit equal to the configuration, or no limit at all, is taken as is.

## Destroy

The API has no delete. Destroying the resource leaves the limit at Mistral as it is, and Terraform says so in a warning. Removing the limit instead would lift a cost cap as a side effect of a destroy, and the limit the organization had before Terraform is not known, so it could not be restored. To remove the limit, apply `no_monthly_limit = true` before you destroy the resource.

